  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SINOPLAST II, Sino-Norwegian cooperation on capacity building for reducing plastic and microplastic pollution</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SINOPLAST II aims to develop necessary tools to improve the capacities of plastic management in China and thus increase China&#x2019;s preparedness for upcoming international agreement on plastics. The project is implemented by the Ministry of Ecology and Environment of the People&apos;s Republic of China through the Basel Convention Regional Centre for Asia and the Pacific in China (BCRC China). The Norwegian Institute of Water Research (NIVA) is leading the project on the Norwegian side with support from the Norwegian Environment Agency (NEA). The project includes measurement of female participants.</narrative>
  </description>
